  "text": "Nobody posts the despair part of the journey. So here's mine.\n\nI'm 2 weeks into a 6-week Level 5 Advanced Diploma in Financial Trading with ZISHI, and it's been a process.\n\nIf you've ever started something hard, you'll know the curve:\n\n\t1.\tExcitement\n\t2.\tReality\n\t3.\tDoubt\n\t4.\tDespair\n\t5.\tClarity\n\t6.\tSuccess\n\nWeek 1 was excitement. I was finally sat in front of a professional trading platform, learning from someone who spent decades on the trading floor. Then reality hit fast. Futures, derivatives, asset classes, order types, market participants: it was a whole new language, and I had to learn it in days, not months.\n\nWeek 2 is doubt and despair. Theory turned into live markets, and I started second-guessing everything. I'd wait for the perfect entry, overthink it, then watch the move happen without me.\n\nSo I'm building a process to get through it: volume candles, VWAP, ATR, volume at price, filtering the ladder by contract size, and a daily trading diary.\n\nBiggest lesson so far: waiting for the perfect trade isn't patience, it's fear.\n\nGrateful to Mark Boardman DipPFS for teaching us the process and sharing insights that have already changed how I look at the markets, and to Robert Russell for his mentorship and the standard he sets for everyone on the course."
