  "post": "https://lnkd.in/p/gpFY75sD",
  "date": "2026-08-25",
  "text": "Final Week at ZISHI Completed - Level 5 Advanced Diploma in Financial Trading.\n\nFinishing the Advanced Level 5 Trading Diploma Programme, accredited by #VTCT and recognised by #CISI at Associate Membership level, has been one of the most transformative experiences of my academic and professional journey. Looking back to where I started five weeks ago, the difference in my mindset, confidence, and capability is something I am genuinely proud of.\n\nWhen I first entered the trading room, I felt unsure of what the next five weeks would hold. I arrived with enthusiasm, but without a full understanding of the discipline, resilience, and emotional control that professional trading demands. This programme has changed that completely. It has revealed the true nature of trading, the pressure involved, the speed of decision making, the responsibility behind every action, and the behaviours required to succeed in the long term.\n\nI also want to highlight something important. The trading room is a safe and supportive environment for women. It is professional, structured, and encouraging, and it is nothing like the stereotypes shown online. I felt supported every step of the way.\n\nThe friendships formed during this programme have been just as valuable. Working alongside people who are committed and driven has shaped my experience and strengthened my emotional intelligence. We have supported each other, challenged each other, and progressed together.\n\nA special thank you to Jon Harman, my mentor for the final week, whose guidance helped bring everything together. I also want to thank Robert Russell, Alex Wilson, and David Michael for their continuous support and for teaching us far beyond charts and theory. Their mentorship has shaped how I think, how I prepare, and how I behave in a professional environment.\n\nThank you to ZISHI, ICE, Aralyx Trading, and Sheffield Hallam University for sponsoring this programme. I am proud to have completed this qualification, and I am grateful for the opportunity.\n\nI recommend this programme to anyone who wants to understand the realities of trading and develop the mindset needed for a professional career. It is one of the best decisions I have made.\n\nZISHI Sheffield Hallam University Sheffield Business School SBS ICE Aralyx Trading\n\n#ZISHI #SBS #Sheffieldhallamuniversity #ICE #AralyxTrading #VTCT #TradingTechnologies #CISI"
