  "text": "Week 4 of my Level 5 Advanced Diploma in Financial Trading with ZISHI at Sheffield Business School is complete.\nThis week the focus shifted from just applying the theory to incorporating it day to day. Time management has been a big area of growth, hitting deadlines for our diaries and being set challenges while still giving full attention to the trading room. One key takeaway was learning to trade within set budgets and using bracket orders, a small but important shift that has made me far more disciplined about defining risk before I even enter a position, rather than managing it after the fact. My attention to detail is improving too, taking in more information during live sessions and getting better at deciding what actually matters versus noise. Planning and research before each session is becoming second nature, and I am seeing real progress in my control over positions and appreciation of risk.\nWorking both individually and as part of a team has tested different skills, from taking ownership of my own decisions to supporting others when it counted. The environment continues to bring out qualities I did not know I had: resilience, discipline, patience, and a competitive edge that pushes me to prepare properly for every session. It is demanding, but that is exactly why it is building the work ethic and leadership skills I came onto this programme to develop.\nHalfway through the final week now, and I cannot believe where the time has gone. I am proud of how far my discipline and decision-making have come since week 1.\nA huge thank you to Robert Russell, George Lake, Alex Wilson, Jon Harman and David Michael for their continued guidance, and to the programme sponsors for making this possible.\n#Zishi #SBS #SheffieldHallamUniversity #ICE #FinancialTrading #ProfessionalDevelopment #CISI #RiskManagement #TradingTechnologies"
