  "text": "WEEK 4 REFLECTION\n\nI have now completed the fourth week of the Level 5 Advanced Diploma in Financial Trading with ZISHI at Sheffield Hallam University.\n\nThis week, everything began to connect. My greatest development has not simply been gaining technical knowledge, but changing how I behave in the trading room. Preparation, discipline, patience, resilience and accountability are becoming natural parts of my approach.\n\nI now conduct thorough research and only enter a market when I have a clear reason and sufficient confidence in the opportunity. Before an interest rate announcement or major economic release, I consider how different outcomes could affect equities, bonds and currencies. I prepare several trading scenarios in advance, then wait for the figures and market reaction before acting.\n\nMy trading diary has helped me identify patterns in my performance and understand how emotions can influence my decisions. I am learning to recognise fear, overconfidence and uncertainty without allowing them to control my trades. Sometimes the most disciplined decision is to wait or not trade at all.\n\nI have also become more adaptable by exploring different markets, including cocoa, coffee, the Nikkei and the British pound. Rather than forcing the same strategy every day, I now adjust my plan when market conditions change. I also developed my understanding of using spreads to hedge risk and when options may be appropriate. We explored how fear and greed influence market behaviour, including using the VIX to assess expected volatility and the level of fear in the market.\n\nA special thank you to David Michael for being a great mentor and making difficult subjects feel “easier than falling in love”. His teaching on fundamental analysis, options and spreads has made complex ideas much easier to apply.\n\nThank you also to Robert Russell for his technical analysis session, which strengthened my understanding of entry and exit points, Fibonacci retracements, Bollinger Bands, RSI and MACD. I would also like to thank Neil Scurlock for sharing the history of ICE, explaining how exchanges operate and providing valuable career and job application advice.\n\nI remain grateful to ZISHI, ICE, Aralyx, Sheffield Hallam University and Sheffield Business School for making this opportunity possible. Thank you also to Trading Technologies for providing access to its platform.\n\nWeek 4 has strengthened my ability to analyse market conditions, control my emotions, adapt my strategy and manage risk. These behaviours are helping me become a more disciplined and consistent trader who can make informed decisions under pressure.\n\nI cannot believe there is only one week left!\n\n#ZISHI #SBS #SheffieldHallamUniversity #ICE #AralyxTrading #VTCT #TradingTechnologies #CISI"
